Pasi Kallinen wrote:
> Olsonea <olsonea@gmail.com> wrote:
> > Can I use arrays within menucolor statements in the Win32 version? My
> > menucolor options from NAO do not seem to work, specifically, the ones
> > with arrays. 0% and 100% works fine, as does the * and ? wildcards.
> > Does anyone know why the functionality could be different?
> >
> > MENUCOLOR="* 0%"=lightgreen
>
> Because the version of NAO was compiled with regex-support, whereas
> your Win32 version only has the nethack's internal globbing support.
> (So it only supports ? and * wildcards)
>
> See the MENU_COLOR_REGEX and MENU_COLOR_REGEX_POSIX -defines in
> include/config.h
